  "final_message": "**Root cause:** In `refund_invoice` (`billing/refunds.py`), the code called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function expects an invoice ID and looks payments up by invoice. Passing the customer ID found no payments, so the refund total stayed at 0 and the \"no successful payment\" error was raised.\n\n**Fix:** `refund_invoice` now passes `invoice_id`. Tests (24) and ruff pass, but none of the existing tests exercise this bug, and I didn't add one.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` as `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`.",
